course: dictionary
lesson: 1430
title: Carol: a song, a sing, a name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one is meant. «Carol» can be a noun, a verb, or a name.
explain: «The field-mice sing an old carol about standing in the cold and snow.» Can you sing a carol? Yes, so here a carol is a song. Test it: "They sing an old song about the cold and snow" still makes sense.
explain: «It's the field-mice, out carol-singing, as they do every year.» Here carol is a verb: the mice are going about and singing. A capital C, as in Carol, is a girl's name, and you can spot it because it is a person.
fact: A carol is a happy song, often sung at Christmas.
fact: To carol means to sing happily, or to go from house to house singing Christmas songs.
fact: Carol is also a girl's name, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: In Ukraine, «kolyadky» are carols: children go from house to house singing them, and the hosts give sweets or coins.
fact: Christmas carol, carol singers and carol service are all phrases you may hear at Christmas.
exercise: «The field-mice sing an old carol about standing in the cold and snow.» In this sentence, what is a carol? | *A song | A church bell | A kind of mouse | A cold, snowy field
exercise: «It's the field-mice, out carol-singing, as they do every year.» What is carol-singing? | Swimming in a cold river | Reading old books aloud | *Going from house to house singing Christmas songs | Whispering secrets in the dark
exercise: Which word is a girl's name? «Carol and her brother sang at the school concert.» | concert | *Carol | brother | sang
test: In «The Wind in the Willows» the field-mice sing carols in the snow. What does carols mean here? | *Songs | Cold winds | Church bells | Stories about badgers
test: «Kolyadky» are sung from house to house in Ukraine. What does kolyadky mean? | Sweets given to children | Church bells | Snowy fields | *Carols
exam: Which meaning of carol fits the title «Carol of the Bells»? | A girl's name | A film about America | *A song | A kind of bell
